<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies frost free Tuesday, some showers.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies frost free Tuesday, some showers.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies were free of any overnight frost Tuesday morning as clouds and scattered showers were forecast for the region, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Manitoba was the coldest part of the Prairies this morning with lows ranging between 6.0 and 9.0 Celsius, meteorologist Phil Wright said.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see mainly sunny skies in the east, a mix of sun and cloud in the west with highs of 17 to 22 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see mainly cloudy skies with some rain and highs of 12 to 20 Celsius.</p>
<p>Alberta should see some rain, highs of 12 to 16 Celsius.</p>
<p>The normal high at this time of year is 17 Celsius.</p>
<p>--Gilbert Le Gras 204-947-3548</p>
